# Firebase Web App configuration.
#
# Local development: copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values from
# Firebase console -> Project settings -> Your apps -> SDK setup and config.
#
# CI / production: these are set as GitHub Actions *repository variables* of the
# same names (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions -> Variables). They
# are public client identifiers rather than secrets — access is enforced by
# firestore.rules — but they are deliberately never committed, because the
# pre-commit scanner treats an inline API key as a leak.
#
# All six are required. `vite build` fails if any are missing, so a production
# bundle can never be shipped pointing at the wrong project or none at all.
# Without them the app still runs, degraded to local-only storage with no
# sign-in or cloud sync.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
